---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BlogPosting",
  "headline": "7 Best TED Talks About Communication, Public Speaking & Active Listening",
  "description": "Master verbal clarity, body language, and deep listening with the best TED talks about communication. Featuring Julian Treasure, Amy Cuddy, and Celeste Headlee.",
  "image": "https://img.youtube.com/vi/eIho2S0ZahI/hqdefault.jpg",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-24T00:00:00Z",
  "dateModified": "2026-10-24T00:00:00Z",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "TED Talk Finder Editorial",
    "url": "https://tedtalksfinder.com/"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "TED Talk Finder",
    "url": "https://tedtalksfinder.com/"
  },
  "mainEntityOfPage": {
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": "https://tedtalksfinder.com/blog/best-ted-talks-communication"
  }
};

const breadcrumbSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Home",
      "item": "https://tedtalksfinder.com"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 2,
      "name": "Blog",
      "item": "https://tedtalksfinder.com/blog"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 3,
      "name": "Communication",
      "item": "https://tedtalksfinder.com/blog/best-ted-talks-communication"
    }
  ]
};
---

<Layout
  title="7 Best TED Talks About Communication & Active Listening (Ranked)"
  description="Discover the best TED talks about communication to transform your speaking, active listening, and executive presence. Featuring Julian Treasure and Celeste Headlee."
  canonicalUrl="https://tedtalksfinder.com/blog/best-ted-talks-communication"
>
  <Header activePage="blog" />

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema)} />

  <main class="flex-grow bg-white py-10 sm:py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 md:px-12">
    <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-6 text-[10px] sm:text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-500 font-semibold flex items-center gap-2">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-black">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <a href="/blog" class="hover:text-black">Blog</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-[#EB0028]">Communication</span>
      </nav>

      <!-- Article Header -->
      <header class="border-b border-gray-200 pb-8 mb-10 space-y-4">
        <span class="inline-block bg-black text-white text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider font-extrabold px-3 py-1">
          Communication &amp; Public Speaking
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold uppercase tracking-tight text-black leading-tight">
          7 Best TED Talks About Communication, Public Speaking &amp; Active Listening
        </h1>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-xs text-gray-500 pt-2 font-medium">
          <span>By <strong>TED Talk Finder Editorial</strong></span>
          <span>•</span>
          <time datetime="2026-10-24">October 24, 2026</time>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>6 min read</span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- Article Body -->
      <div class="prose-content space-y-8 text-gray-800 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed font-normal">
          Whether you are delivering a keynote, pitching an investor, or having a delicate conversation with a colleague, communication is the single highest-leverage skill in the modern world. If you are looking for the <strong>best TED talks about communication</strong>, you are in good company — millions of executives, researchers, and learners watch these talks each month to refine their conversational mastery.
        </p>

        <p>
          Here are the most authoritative TED talks on vocal authority, posture, active listening, and interpersonal connection.
        </p>

        <!-- Talk 1 -->
        <section class="border border-gray-200 p-6 sm:p-8 bg-gray-50 space-y-4">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-2 border-b border-gray-200 pb-4">
            <div>
              <span class="text-[10px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#EB0028]">Talk #1</span>
              <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-black mt-1">
                How to Speak So That People Want to Listen — Julian Treasure
              </h2>
            </div>
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-500">10 min • 53M+ Views</span>
          </div>

          <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Sound and acoustic expert Julian Treasure breaks down why people often tune us out and provides a simple, actionable toolkit for commanding respect without shouting. He introduces the four cornerstones of powerful speech under the acronym <strong>HAIL</strong>: Honesty, Authenticity, Integrity, and Love.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 p-4 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-black">Core Takeaways:</h3>
            <ul class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-700 list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
              <li>Avoid the 7 deadly sins of speaking: gossip, judging, negativity, complaining, excuses, exaggeration, and dogmatism.</li>
              <li>Harness the vocal engine: master register (speaking from the chest), timbre, prosody, pace, and strategic silence.</li>
              <li>Silence is not dead air; pausing conveys immense poise and commands audience focus.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <a
            href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eIho2S0ZahI"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-block bg-[#EB0028] hover:bg-[#c40020] text-white text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider px-6 py-3 transition-colors"
          >
            Watch Julian Treasure on YouTube →
          </a>
        </section>

        <!-- Talk 2 -->
        <section class="border border-gray-200 p-6 sm:p-8 bg-gray-50 space-y-4">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-2 border-b border-gray-200 pb-4">
            <div>
              <span class="text-[10px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#EB0028]">Talk #2</span>
              <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-black mt-1">
                10 Ways to Have a Better Conversation — Celeste Headlee
              </h2>
            </div>
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-500">12 min • 33M+ Views</span>
          </div>

          <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Seasoned radio host Celeste Headlee emphasizes that conversation requires a balance between talking and listening, an art which many of us have lost in the age of texting and social media polarization.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 p-4 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-black">Core Takeaways:</h3>
            <ul class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-700 list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
              <li>Don't multitask: be present in the moment or don't engage.</li>
              <li>Use open-ended questions: start with Who, What, Where, When, Why, or How.</li>
              <li>Don't equate your experience with theirs: if they talk about losing a parent, don't hijack the moment with your story. It's not about you.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <a
            href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R1vskiVDwl4"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-block bg-[#EB0028] hover:bg-[#c40020] text-white text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider px-6 py-3 transition-colors"
          >
            Watch Celeste Headlee on YouTube →
          </a>
        </section>

        <!-- Talk 3 -->
        <section class="border border-gray-200 p-6 sm:p-8 bg-gray-50 space-y-4">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-2 border-b border-gray-200 pb-4">
            <div>
              <span class="text-[10px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#EB0028]">Talk #3</span>
              <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-black mt-1">
                Your Body Language May Shape Who You Are — Amy Cuddy
              </h2>
            </div>
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-500">21 min • 70M+ Views</span>
          </div>

          <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Nonverbal communication doesn't just inform how listeners perceive you; it fundamentally impacts how you perceive yourself. Amy Cuddy demonstrates how holding expansive postures ("power posing") for two minutes prior to high-stakes meetings reduces cortisol and increases confidence.
          </p>

          <a
            href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ks-_Mh1QhMc"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-block bg-[#EB0028] hover:bg-[#c40020] text-white text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider px-6 py-3 transition-colors"
          >
            Watch Amy Cuddy on YouTube →
          </a>
        </section>

        <!-- Call to Action -->
        <div class="bg-black text-white p-8 sm:p-10 border border-gray-900 mt-12 space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black uppercase tracking-tight">
            Find Hundreds of Communication Talks Instantly
          </h2>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Looking for talks on storytelling, active listening, or overcoming social anxiety? Use our AI search engine to uncover talks curated directly from official TED sources.
          </p>
          <div class="pt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
            <a
              href="/?q=communication"
              class="bg-[#EB0028] hover:bg-[#c40020] text-white text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider px-6 py-3 transition-colors"
            >
              Search "Communication" Talks →
            </a>
            <a
              href="/blog/best-ted-talks-philosophy-life"
              class="border border-gray-700 hover:border-white text-white text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider px-6 py-3 transition-colors"
            >
              Read: Philosophy &amp; Life Talks
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
